<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">People's Front for Democracy and Justice</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1994</span> · Also known as PFDJ</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The People's Front for Democracy and Justice is the ruling and only legal party of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eritrea">Eritrea</a>, formed in February 1994 from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eritrean-peoples-liberation-front">Eritrean People's Liberation Front</a>, which had won the war of independence against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>. Led by President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isaias-afwerki">Isaias Afwerki</a>, it has governed without national elections since independence, under a constitution ratified in 1997 but never implemented.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peoples-front-for-democracy-and-justice.jpg" alt="People's Front for Democracy and Justice" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Permjak · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_EPLF.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
